  "description": "VOJQIY crystallizes in the cubic crystal system with space group P n -3 n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C160 H154 Eu8 O42 Yb1 1+,Cl1 1-. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Yb1 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1B (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1E (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1G (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1H (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1I (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1V (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1W (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2? (Yb) has 0 O neighbors; Eu2? (Eu) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.651-5.164 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.50-169.23°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Eu8Yb(BA)16(OH)10]Cl (BA = benzoylacetonate); crystal solvate also given as [Eu8Yb(BA)16(OH)10]Cl·3(C2H5OH)·4(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 10 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 10 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 10 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
